# Extensions

Framework extensions own reusable application composition. A plugin contributes to an application plan; a custom application protocol defines preparation, runtime, scopes, and endpoint serving. Axum WebSocket protocol implementations remain under Axum because they own that server wire contract.

## Choose a task

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| package components and declarations as one inspectable unit | <GuideRef slug="framework/extensions/plugins">Compose plugins</GuideRef> |
| define a new application-level dispatch and serving model | <GuideRef slug="framework/extensions/protocol-authoring">Protocol authoring</GuideRef> |
| implement WebSocket framing, dispatch, and subprotocol negotiation | <GuideRef slug="axum/websocket/protocol-authoring">Axum WebSocket protocol authoring</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Understand the <GuideRef slug="framework/application/protocol-composition">one-protocol application invariant</GuideRef> and use stable IDs for anything that must be inspected or composed across packages.
